\section{Conclusion and Future Works}
In this paper, we propose \textit{DecoyDB}, a comprehensive dataset of high-resolution 3D complexes augmented with decoys for pretraining graph neural networks in protein-ligand binding affinity prediction. We also design a customized GCL algorithm based on DecoyDB. Experiments show that pre-training on DecoyDB improves multiple base models in prediction accuracy, sample learning efficiency, and model generalizability. 

In the future, we plan to extend the proposed framework to other tasks beyond binding affinity prediction, such as binding pose estimation and drug generation.  


