\subsection{Stimulation Mapping Results}
\vspace{-0.075in}
Stimulation mapping was performed across all electrodes of the ECoG grid. Stimulation parameters that elicited hand and leg sensory responses and the subjects' verbal descriptions are reported in Table~\ref{tab:stim_map}, and topographically portrayed in Fig. \ref{fig:coreg}. Note that while the sensory mapping was more extensive, only examples of salient responses were reported here. Also, some motor responses (involuntary movement) were also elicited during the mapping procedure. Channels with motor responses at any stimulation parameter set were excluded from this list. For all subjects, the most common artificial sensation was a tingling sensation.  

