\subsection{The Mayer-Vietoris sequence in coarse cohomology}


The Mayer-Vietoris sequence in coarse cohomology is more subtle. 
We start with the following lemma.

\begin{lemma}
\label{LemmaCohHalfMV}
Let $\cX$ and $\cY$ be two big families in a proper metric space $M$.
Then the sequence of cochain complexes
\begin{equation}
\label{SESCohomology}
\begin{tikzcd}[column sep=0.8cm]
0 \ar[r]
&
CX^\bullet(\cX \Cup \cY) \ar[r]
&
CX^\bullet(\cX) \oplus CX^\bullet( \cY)
\ar[r]
&
CX^\bullet(\cX \Cap \cY)
\end{tikzcd}
\end{equation}
is exact, where the maps are dual to those of the homological Mayer-Vietoris sequence.
\end{lemma}

