\begin{equation*}%\label{MVDifferentialFormula}
\delta_{\mathrm{MV}}([\theta]) = [\delta(\tilde{\theta})] = -[\delta(\tilde{\theta}^c)], 
\end{equation*}
where on the right hand side, $\delta$ is the Alexander-Spanier differential.
From the exactness of the sequence of cochain complexes, it follows that $\delta(\tilde{\theta})$ and $-\delta(\tilde{\theta}^c)$  agree and are actually contained in $CX^{n+1}_\alpha(\cZ)$.
\end{remark}



