\subsection{ The root system $\widetilde G_2$} 
\label{AppendixB.4}


Let $V$ be the hyperplane in $\mathbb R^3$ consisting of all vectors whose coordinates add up to $0$. 
The $G_2$-root system  is  the set of vectors in $V$ with integer coordinates and of length  $\sqrt2$ or $\sqrt6$
 given by 
 \[
\mathcal G_2=\{ \pm(\epsilon_i-\epsilon_j) \mid  { 1\leq i < j \leq 3}\}\cup \{ \pm(2\epsilon_i-\epsilon_j-\epsilon_k)  \mid { 1 \leq i, j,k \leq 3 }\}\ . 
\]
It has natural simple roots given by 
$\alpha_1=\epsilon_1-\epsilon_2$ and $\alpha_2=-2\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_2+\epsilon_3$.  The highest root can be written  according to  $
\overline{\alpha}=3\alpha_1+2\alpha_2 = -\epsilon_1 - \epsilon_2 +2\epsilon_3\ $. 

