As the systems evolved, distinct temporal trends emerged. By $t = 100$, the stable system maintained consistent entropy levels ($H(u+v) = 6.489512$ bits, spatial entropy $3.670517 \pm 0.382467$ bits), while the turbulent system showed increased complexity ($H(u+v) = 6.600704$ bits, spatial entropy $3.660448 \pm 0.403447$ bits). Notably, the mutual information decreased in both systems but more dramatically in the turbulent case: from initial values to $I(U;V) = 4.304781$ bits (normalized: 0.663998) for stable and $I(U;V) = 3.691138$ bits (normalized: 0.564959) for turbulent dynamics.

