Meanwhile, financials and industrials sectors exhibit weak extremal
dependence {between the two countries}. Although financial markets are
globally linked, China's 
capital controls and state-regulated banking limit direct
spillovers. However, interest rate changes, trade tensions, and
economic downturns may still affect financial institutions in both
