\section{Correction of Surface Wind Speed}\label{sec:wind_results}

\subsection{Analysis of Path Signature Outputs}\label{sec:wind_sig_analysis}
The NWP dataset consists of surface wind speed structured as a space-time array of size $(49, 68, 695),$ with $49 \times 68 = 3,332$ spatial gridpoints, and $695$ time-steps. To increase the sample size for NN training, simulations  are reorganized into 15-hour intervals (46 samples) rather than daily 24-hour segments (29 samples). 
The depth-1 path signature is computed at each of the 3,332 gridpoints of the NWP model outputs for a dyadic window of depth 3. As previously, PCA is applied on the resulting path signature, retaining 41 components that explain 99.5$\%$ of the total variance. 
