%\smallskip

%\noindent Suppose not. Then $F \subset \mathcal{S} \setminus \{k\}$. Since $k$ is a cut point of $G_{([n] \setminus \mathcal{S}) \cup \{k\}}$, it follows that $G_{[n] \setminus F}$ is connected, contradicting $F \in \min(G)$.

%\smallskip

