Since we already know that $B_1 \in \mathcal{D}_{c}(G_1)$, it suffices to verify that each $x \in \mathcal{S}$ is adjacent to some vertex in $B_1$. Suppose not, and let $x \in \mathcal{S}$ be such that $\{x, b\} \notin E(G)$ for all $b \in B_1$. Define $A := [n] \setminus (B_1 \cup V_2 \cup \{x\})$.

