Our next objective is to determine the initial ideal of $(J_{C_n} : f_{i-1,i+1})$. %To this end, we begin by computing the ideal $(J_{C_n} : f_{i-1,i+1})$ itself.

\begin{lemma}\label{saturation with f}
The initial ideal of the saturation $(J_{C_n} : f_{i-1,i+1})$ satisfies
\[
\mathrm{in}_{<}((J_{C_n} : f_{i-1,i+1})) = \mathrm{in}_{<}(J_{C_n}) + (x_i, y_i) + \left( g_{C,D} \,\middle|\, C \cup D = [n] \setminus \{i-1, i, i+1\},\; C \cap D = \emptyset \right).
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
By applying Theorem~3.7 and Lemma~3.8 from \cite{mohammadi2014hilbert} to our setting, we obtain the following decomposition:
\[
(J_{C_n} : f_{i-1,i+1}) =  J_{C_n} + (x_i, y_i) + \left( g_{C,D} \,\middle|\, C \cup D = [n] \setminus \{i-1, i, i+1\},\; C \cap D = \emptyset \right).
\]
Let
\[
