    $$\mathbb{P}(\LNS_{N_t}\ge t(p_j+3\varepsilon))\le \mathbb{P}(\mathcal{H}^{(\alpha_t)}_t\ge  t(p_j+\varepsilon))+\mathbb{P}(\sum_{i\notin I} K^{(\alpha_t)}_i \ge t\varepsilon)+\mathbb{P}(\sum_{i\in I} K^{(\alpha_t)}_i \ge t\varepsilon)$$
\end{proof}
Since $\mathcal{H}^{(\alpha_t)}_t$ is a poisson random variable with parameter $t\alpha_t \le t(p_j+\varepsilon/2)$ for $t$ large enough, we have
$$ \mathbb{P}(\mathcal{H}^{(\alpha_t)}_t\ge  t(p_j+\varepsilon))\le \exp(-c_1 t)$$
for some for some constant $c_1$ (depending on $p_j$  and $\varepsilon$).
The random variable  $K^{(\alpha_t)}_i$ is a geometric random variable with parameter $1-\frac{p_i}{\alpha_t}$, thus for   $i \notin $I, it is dominated by a  geometric random variable  with parameter $1-\frac{p_i}{p_j}$. Hence considering $Y=\sum_{i\notin I} \bar{K_i}$ where  $(\bar{K_i})_{i\notin I}$ are independent and $\mathcal{G}_{\ge 0}(1-\frac{p_i}{p_j})$, we get 
$$\mathbb{P}(\sum_{i\notin I} K^{(\alpha_t)}_i \ge t\varepsilon)\le \mathbb{P}(Y\ge t\varepsilon)\le \frac{\mbox{Var}(Y)}{\varepsilon^2t^2}$$
Besides
$$\mbox{Var}(Y)=\sum_{i\notin I} \frac{p_jp_i}{(p_j-p_i)^2}\le \frac{p_j}{\min_{i\notin I}(p_j-p_i)^2}<\infty$$


$$\mathbb{P}(\sum_{i\in I} K^{(\alpha_t)}_i \ge t\varepsilon)\le |I|\mathbb{P}( K^{(\alpha_t)}_j \ge t\frac{\varepsilon}{|I|})=|I|(1-\frac{1}{\sqrt{t}p_j+1})^{t\frac{\varepsilon}{|I|}}\le c_2\exp(-c_3\sqrt{t})$$
