\autoref{main-2} has the following two immediate corollaries.  

First, for the regularity $k> 7/2$, we are able to formulate a {\em complete criterion} of sphericity:

\begin{theorem}
\Label{main-2-iff}
Let
$M\subset\CC{2}$
be a strictly pseudoconvex real hypersurface 
of class $C^k,\,k> 7/2$
and $L$ a (nonzero) regularizing
$(0,1)$
vector field on $M$ of class $C^1$.
Then $M$
is spherical
at a point $p$
 if and only if
\beq
\Label{main-cond1}
L\Phi, L^2\Phi, L^3\Phi \in C^1,
\quad
L^4 \Phi =0.
\eeq
\end{theorem}

Second, in the "super low" regularity $2\leq k\leq 7/2$, we can formulate a sufficient condition for sphericity.

\begin{corollary}
\Label{main-2-suff}
Let
$M\subset\CC{2}$
be a strictly pseudoconvex real hypersurface 
of class $C^k,\,2\leq k\leq 7/2,$
and $L$ a (nonzero) regularizing
$(0,1)$
vector field on $M$ of class $C^1$.
Then $M$
is spherical
at a point $p$
 if 
\begin{equation}
\Label{main-cond2}
\Phi,L\Phi, L^2\Phi, L^3\Phi \in C^1,
\quad
L^4 \Phi =0.
\end{equation}
\end{corollary}

