Finally, we have an application of \autoref{main-2} directly to the Cartan-Tanaka-Chern-Moser theory (in low regularity). Precisely, we prove the following result with optimal regularity:

\begin{theorem}\Label{zerocurv}
A strictly pseudoconvex hypersurface $M\subset\CC{2}$ of class $C^6$ is spherical if and only if its Cartan invariant (the CR curvature) vanishes on $M$.    
\end{theorem}

Note that $6$ is precisely the number of derivatives needed to define the CR curvature in $\C^2$, 
hence the regularity order $6$ is optimal.
On the other hand,
as discussed above, this result can {\em not} be deduced from Cartan-Tanaka-Chern-Moser theory,
which requires higher order differentiation
to conclude sphericity by standard methods.

