We now make use of the following remarkable fact, going back to the work of E.~Cartan and A.~Tresse. 
We refer to e.g. \cite{divergence} for more details. 
\begin{proposition}\Label{cubicODE}
A Levi-nondegenerate real-analytic hypersurface $M\subset\CC{2}$ is spherical if and only if the defining function $\Phi$ of its associated ODE  \eqref{wzz} is cubic with respect to the the jet coordinate $\xi:=w'$.  
\end{proposition}


