values at finitely many points
by means of the Lagrange interpolation formula,
which provides the same regularity
as restrictions of $\Phi$ for fixed values of $\xi$.

Extending 
the CR functions $a_0,...,a_3$
holomorphically to the pseudoconvex side
and using the uniqueness of holomorphic extension,
we finally obtain:
\beq\Label{condit}
\Phi
=a_0+a_1\theta+a_2\theta^2+a_3\theta^3,
\eeq
where 
%we still write $a_j$ for their holomorphic 
$\theta$ is as in \eqref{th-def},\eqref{th-coor}. 
