Then the solution of~\eqref{eqn:euler_phi} $(V,w,\rho,\eta_0)$ given by Theorem~\ref{thm:euler_phi} is in $C^0([0,\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon}) T],H^{s}(S)^{d+2} \times H^s(\R^d))$.
