We expect long-term improvements to neutrino detection using the IceCube Neutrino Observatory with the implementation of the IceCube Upgrade, currently being installed at the South Pole. The IceCube Upgrade will extend IceCube's neutrino sensitivity to even lower energies (GeV and below) by increasing the density of the infill array's (IceCube DeepCore) strings \cite{Ishihara:2019uL}. On a more long-term timescale, IceCube Gen-2 will provide increased instrument volume and the addition of Gen-2 Radio which, when combined, will extend improved sensitivity to the TeV-PeV energy range for high-energy neutrino emission from nearby supernovae \cite{IceCube-Gen2:2020qha}. 
